      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Food shops must follow the Food Safety Act 1990 and the Food Hygiene (England) Regulations 2013. They need a food safety system based on HACCP.</li><li>Due diligence means keeping proof: temperature logs, date checks, cleaning records and allergen information.</li><li>Natasha's Law and the Food Information Regulations set the rules on allergen labels.</li><li>The Food Hygiene Rating depends a lot on the records.</li><li>The audit does not keep food safe. The controls do. Quickler captures the records with times and photos.</li></ul>"
